+/* sb-patches/0126 (docs/WIN11-GPU.md 6.42): file switches under C:\ProgramData\Starbite (every process sees them,
+ * DWM and the shell included, unlike environment variables), this process's image name, and the resource canary. */
+int
+malikm_switch(const char *name)
+{
+   char p[MAX_PATH];
+   snprintf(p, sizeof(p), "C:\\ProgramData\\Starbite\\%s", name);
+   return GetFileAttributesA(p) != INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES;
+}
+
+const char *
+malikm_exe(void)
+{
+   static char b[64];
+   if (!b[0]) {
+      char exe[MAX_PATH];
+      GetModuleFileNameA(NULL, exe, sizeof(exe));
+      const char *s = strrchr(exe, '\\');
+      snprintf(b, sizeof(b), "%s", s ? s + 1 : exe);
+   }
+   return b;
+}
+
+/* A panfrost_resource that a batch was about to read or write is not a live one (freed, or never one): logged with
+ * the caller's offset in this DLL (maps/sbumd.map names it) and skipped instead of dereferenced (T30's Explorer
+ * crash: pan_resource_afbcp_update +0xc on a freed resource). */
+void
+malikm_canary(const char *what, const void *rsrc, unsigned magic, const void *ret)
+{
+   static volatile LONG n;
+   LONG c = InterlockedIncrement(&n);
+   malikm_note_count(29);                 /* UmdNote_29: canary hits */
+   if (c <= 32 || (c & (c - 1)) == 0) {
+      HMODULE m = NULL;
+      GetModuleHandleExA(GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_FROM_ADDRESS | GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_UNCHANGED_REFCOUNT,
+                         (LPCSTR)(void *)malikm_canary, &m);
+      fprintf(stderr, "sbumd: CANARY %s: resource %p magic 0x%08x is not a live resource; called from rva 0x%llx; "
+              "skipped (hit %ld)\n", what, rsrc, magic, (unsigned long long)((uintptr_t)ret - (uintptr_t)m), c);
+      fflush(stderr);
+   }
+}
